There's no good reason to deal with shopkeepers in NHK 3.1.  What good
are they to the average adventurer?  They're obsequious if you're good
looking, sell you dodgy and cursed items, rake at least a 100% profit
on trade-ins, and call the Kops if you steal anything.

Here's a couple of fun suggestions for increasing interaction with
shopkeepers:

1. Allow shopkeepers to restock.  In NHK 3.1, once shopkeepers run out
of stock, I let my pet kill them for money to donate to my priest.

2. Have shopkeepers provide services.  These services can be
identifying items (eg. jewellers for rings, butlers for potions),
increasing your charisma (hairdressers), teach you the spells (mages),
improve your wisdom (monks), make weapons (blacksmiths), heal you
(doctors) and increase your dexterity (guru).  Services can be provided
by providing the necessary materials and paying zorkmids for labour.

